WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:03.030
- [Joma] Thanks to IBM for
sponsoring a part of this video.

00:00:03.030 --> 00:00:04.050
- [Dio] My name is Dio

00:00:04.050 --> 00:00:06.360
and I was on track for a return offer,

00:00:06.360 --> 00:00:08.600
until one day he showed up.

00:00:08.600 --> 00:00:09.433
(ominous music)

00:00:09.433 --> 00:00:12.240
A newly recruited intern
appeared out of nowhere,

00:00:12.240 --> 00:00:13.944
a shadow from my past.

00:00:13.944 --> 00:00:16.620
(ominous music continues)

00:00:16.620 --> 00:00:19.200
His name was Jojoma.

00:00:19.200 --> 00:00:20.550
- [Jojoma] You must be Dio.

00:00:21.750 --> 00:00:23.400
- Yeah, and you are?

00:00:23.400 --> 00:00:24.720
- [Jojoma] You know who I am.

00:00:24.720 --> 00:00:25.590
- What?

00:00:25.590 --> 00:00:26.970
- Do you really think I'd forget

00:00:26.970 --> 00:00:29.956
what you've taken from me, brother?

00:00:29.956 --> 00:00:31.890
♪ Let's ♪

00:00:31.890 --> 00:00:33.300
- What are you talking about?

00:00:33.300 --> 00:00:34.500
- 20 years ago,

00:00:34.500 --> 00:00:37.110
a man in crippling debt
sold his firstborn child

00:00:37.110 --> 00:00:38.190
to clear his name,

00:00:38.190 --> 00:00:40.165
to rebuild his life.

00:00:40.165 --> 00:00:41.850
He even got a new child,

00:00:41.850 --> 00:00:44.370
gave him all the love in the world.

00:00:44.370 --> 00:00:45.960
- I had nothing to do with any of this.

00:00:45.960 --> 00:00:50.220
- That man was your father, our father.

00:00:50.220 --> 00:00:51.900
You stole my life,

00:00:51.900 --> 00:00:54.690
and I'm here to take it all back,

00:00:54.690 --> 00:00:58.003
starting with a Kodocharenji.

00:00:58.003 --> 00:00:58.836
(metal screeches)

00:00:58.836 --> 00:01:01.586
♪ I could change ♪

00:01:02.516 --> 00:01:04.451
(ominous music)

00:01:04.451 --> 00:01:05.730
- Let's talk about IBM.

00:01:05.730 --> 00:01:09.060
IBM believes what businesses
need most to drive progress

00:01:09.060 --> 00:01:11.610
in this next era is creativity.

00:01:11.610 --> 00:01:14.100
Yes, you heard that correctly, creativity.

00:01:14.100 --> 00:01:15.750
I'm not talking about creativity

00:01:15.750 --> 00:01:16.800
in a traditional sense,

00:01:16.800 --> 00:01:18.330
like musicians and artists.

00:01:18.330 --> 00:01:20.160
I'm talking about the developers,

00:01:20.160 --> 00:01:22.380
the data scientists, the visionaries,

00:01:22.380 --> 00:01:24.840
who are creatively applying technology

00:01:24.840 --> 00:01:26.820
in business to drive change.

00:01:26.820 --> 00:01:29.670
IBM calls them New Creators.

00:01:29.670 --> 00:01:32.370
I love this because I've
always believed that technology

00:01:32.370 --> 00:01:34.290
is a tool that we should leverage

00:01:34.290 --> 00:01:37.110
to create real values
in our everyday lives,

00:01:37.110 --> 00:01:38.670
just like these New Creators.

00:01:38.670 --> 00:01:40.440
New Creators think outside the box.

00:01:40.440 --> 00:01:42.750
They are wired to do things differently,

00:01:42.750 --> 00:01:45.600
as long as it makes a positive impact.

00:01:45.600 --> 00:01:48.000
One of the New Creators
I resonate with is Nick.

00:01:48.000 --> 00:01:51.600
He's a Senior Data and AI
Technical Specialist at IBM.

00:01:51.600 --> 00:01:53.520
Nick is passionate about using technology,

00:01:53.520 --> 00:01:55.020
machine learning and data science

00:01:55.020 --> 00:01:56.880
to solve new and novel problems

00:01:56.880 --> 00:01:58.080
that make a difference.

00:01:58.080 --> 00:02:00.180
One example of this is when
he used Computer Vision

00:02:00.180 --> 00:02:02.880
to decode and translate sign language

00:02:02.880 --> 00:02:05.310
in real-time to break
down language barriers

00:02:05.310 --> 00:02:07.590
and create more accessibility online.

00:02:07.590 --> 00:02:09.000
- The main goal is to make the world

00:02:09.000 --> 00:02:10.020
just that little bit better.

00:02:10.020 --> 00:02:10.853
If I can do that,

00:02:10.853 --> 00:02:12.870
then I think my time on this planet

00:02:12.870 --> 00:02:14.040
will have been well served.

00:02:14.040 --> 00:02:17.490
Producing technologies
and using technologies

00:02:17.490 --> 00:02:19.020
for the greater good of humanity,

00:02:19.020 --> 00:02:21.240
I think that's my core goal here.

00:02:21.240 --> 00:02:22.920
- Just like Nick, I
believe in doing things

00:02:22.920 --> 00:02:24.720
that add intrinsic value.

00:02:24.720 --> 00:02:26.730
So to learn more about New Creators,

00:02:26.730 --> 00:02:29.220
you can check out IBM on
their YouTube channel,

00:02:29.220 --> 00:02:30.360
or you could click the link

00:02:30.360 --> 00:02:32.070
in the description down below.

00:02:32.070 --> 00:02:34.170
So again, thank you so much IBM

00:02:34.170 --> 00:02:37.170
for sponsoring this portion of my video.

00:02:37.170 --> 00:02:38.370
- Welcome back, everyone.

00:02:38.370 --> 00:02:42.351
Today's Kodocharenji, we
have Jojoma versus Dio.

00:02:42.351 --> 00:02:43.184
(intense music)

00:02:43.184 --> 00:02:44.017
- [Masked Man] At this company,

00:02:44.017 --> 00:02:46.805
there is one way for interns
to settle their differences.

00:02:46.805 --> 00:02:48.930
A Kodocharenji is a coding battle

00:02:48.930 --> 00:02:52.050
where two interns receive
the same coding challenge.

00:02:52.050 --> 00:02:53.160
They will be judged on their-

00:02:53.160 --> 00:02:55.590
- Speed, efficiency and correctness.

00:02:55.590 --> 00:02:57.990
The winner will receive a return offer,

00:02:57.990 --> 00:03:00.090
but the loser will be kicked out

00:03:00.090 --> 00:03:01.743
of this company immediately.

00:03:02.610 --> 00:03:06.210
Today's challenge: hack
this smart contract.

00:03:06.210 --> 00:03:08.520
- [Dio] Blockchain? Oh, no.

00:03:08.520 --> 00:03:10.860
- You have 60 minutes
to submit your exploit.

00:03:10.860 --> 00:03:12.180
Begin coding.

00:03:12.180 --> 00:03:13.853
Begin coding.

00:03:13.853 --> 00:03:16.920
(intense music)

00:03:16.920 --> 00:03:18.600
- [Masked Man] Dio's
fundamentals are strong.

00:03:18.600 --> 00:03:20.970
This internship has taught
him all the essential skills

00:03:20.970 --> 00:03:23.202
required to becoming an elite engineer.

00:03:23.202 --> 00:03:24.210
(intense music continues)

00:03:24.210 --> 00:03:27.161
Jojoma might be
underestimating his opponent.

00:03:27.161 --> 00:03:32.161
(intense music continues)
(keys clacking)

00:03:36.097 --> 00:03:37.423
(sparks crackling)
(intense music continues)

00:03:37.423 --> 00:03:38.670
(Jojoma exhales)
(Masked Man gasps)

00:03:38.670 --> 00:03:39.503
Nani?

00:03:39.503 --> 00:03:40.920
I've never seen someone so young

00:03:40.920 --> 00:03:42.690
use such an advanced move.

00:03:42.690 --> 00:03:45.806
Is he actually reading documentation?

00:03:45.806 --> 00:03:47.031
(intense music continues)

00:03:47.031 --> 00:03:48.001
(no audio)

00:03:48.001 --> 00:03:49.155
(scroll wheel winding)

00:03:49.155 --> 00:03:52.387
(sparks crackling)

00:03:52.387 --> 00:03:54.030
(intense music)

00:03:54.030 --> 00:03:55.350
- 15 minutes have passed.

00:03:55.350 --> 00:03:57.930
Remember, even if you
found the vulnerability,

00:03:57.930 --> 00:04:00.093
you still have to build out your exploit.

00:04:01.088 --> 00:04:03.794
- [Dio] Oh, no, this is not going well.

00:04:03.794 --> 00:04:05.250
Come on, come on.

00:04:05.250 --> 00:04:06.722
I really need you right now.

00:04:06.722 --> 00:04:08.872
(Dio groans)

00:04:08.872 --> 00:04:09.840
(intense music)

00:04:09.840 --> 00:04:12.390
Yes, the Debugger's Eye allows me

00:04:12.390 --> 00:04:14.340
to quickly see all the possible code paths

00:04:14.340 --> 00:04:16.770
without needing to
compile or run the code.

00:04:16.770 --> 00:04:19.445
This allows me spot bugs
before they even happen.

00:04:19.445 --> 00:04:20.278
(intense music continues)

00:04:20.278 --> 00:04:21.660
- [Masked Man] Dio comes from a long line

00:04:21.660 --> 00:04:22.890
of software developers,

00:04:22.890 --> 00:04:24.870
tracing back to the first developers

00:04:24.870 --> 00:04:26.640
during the Age of Enlightenment,

00:04:26.640 --> 00:04:28.950
who all had the Debugger's Eye.

00:04:28.950 --> 00:04:31.500
This eye gets activated
in times of stress.

00:04:31.500 --> 00:04:33.870
Some say it's an evolutionary adaptation

00:04:33.870 --> 00:04:35.910
for developers to meet their deadlines

00:04:35.910 --> 00:04:39.090
when working with
unreasonable product managers.

00:04:39.090 --> 00:04:41.910
Wait, but these two are brothers.

00:04:41.910 --> 00:04:43.711
That means...

00:04:43.711 --> 00:04:45.840
(intense music)

00:04:45.840 --> 00:04:48.690
Incredible, he has two of them.

00:04:48.690 --> 00:04:49.890
Can it be?

00:04:49.890 --> 00:04:52.710
The Descendant of Codekage himself?

00:04:52.710 --> 00:04:53.880
- 15 minutes left.

00:04:53.880 --> 00:04:56.395
Code submission to the judges is now open.

00:04:56.395 --> 00:05:00.677
(notification chimes)
(intense music)

00:05:00.677 --> 00:05:03.833
(metal screeches)

00:05:03.833 --> 00:05:07.857
(intense music continues)
(keys clack)

00:05:07.857 --> 00:05:10.770
Amazing, Jojoma pulls out another keyboard

00:05:10.770 --> 00:05:12.210
to double his coding speed!

00:05:12.210 --> 00:05:14.195
I've never seen anything like this before.

00:05:14.195 --> 00:05:15.028
(Masked Man gasps)

00:05:15.028 --> 00:05:18.390
- [Masked Man] Impossible,
this dual yielding technique.

00:05:18.390 --> 00:05:19.830
That can only mean he was trained

00:05:19.830 --> 00:05:22.710
in the Hidden Village of Goruden Suteito,

00:05:22.710 --> 00:05:26.034
also known as the San Francisco Bay Area.

00:05:26.034 --> 00:05:26.966
(intense music continues)

00:05:26.966 --> 00:05:28.770
(keys clacking)

00:05:28.770 --> 00:05:30.000
- Once you've completed your challenge,

00:05:30.000 --> 00:05:32.040
you will have to submit
your code to the judges.

00:05:32.040 --> 00:05:34.111
(intense music continues)

00:05:34.111 --> 00:05:36.778
(keys clacking)

00:05:39.256 --> 00:05:41.191
(notification chimes)

00:05:41.191 --> 00:05:42.392
(intense music continues)

00:05:42.392 --> 00:05:45.059
(keys clacking)

00:05:45.985 --> 00:05:49.213
(notification chimes)

00:05:49.213 --> 00:05:53.466
(intense music continues)

00:05:53.466 --> 00:05:54.299
(alarm rings)

00:05:54.299 --> 00:05:55.500
Challenge over!

00:05:55.500 --> 00:05:58.830
We'll now proceed to the
grading phase of this challenge.

00:05:58.830 --> 00:06:01.013
- [Masked Man] Something
doesn't feel right.

00:06:02.053 --> 00:06:04.410
- You know, taking your job offer

00:06:04.410 --> 00:06:05.510
is just the beginning.

00:06:06.420 --> 00:06:08.520
I'm coming for everything.

00:06:08.520 --> 00:06:11.180
- The results are in, the winner is

00:06:11.180 --> 00:06:14.640
(intense music)

00:06:14.640 --> 00:06:15.600
Dio.

00:06:15.600 --> 00:06:16.950
- Nani?
- Masaka!

00:06:16.950 --> 00:06:19.050
- Dio has won by default,

00:06:19.050 --> 00:06:21.295
as Jojoma did not submit his code.

00:06:21.295 --> 00:06:22.128
(intense music)

00:06:22.128 --> 00:06:24.467
- Wait, that's impossible, I sent it.

00:06:24.467 --> 00:06:26.884
(Dio laughs)

00:06:28.590 --> 00:06:29.700
- You did.

00:06:29.700 --> 00:06:30.970
And I received it.

00:06:30.970 --> 00:06:32.378
(intense music)

00:06:32.378 --> 00:06:33.990
- What are you talking about?

00:06:33.990 --> 00:06:35.640
- I spoofed the judge's email,

00:06:35.640 --> 00:06:36.800
and you fell for it.

00:06:36.800 --> 00:06:38.430
(intense music continues)

00:06:38.430 --> 00:06:39.930
You sent your code to me,

00:06:39.930 --> 00:06:42.900
and I took your code and
submitted it for myself.

00:06:42.900 --> 00:06:46.177
(intense music continues)

00:06:46.177 --> 00:06:48.308
(keys clack)

00:06:48.308 --> 00:06:50.850
(intense music continues)

00:06:50.850 --> 00:06:52.740
- Wait, that's cheating.

00:06:52.740 --> 00:06:55.380
You cheated! How's this even allowed?

00:06:55.380 --> 00:06:57.390
- You might have found the vulnerability

00:06:57.390 --> 00:06:59.070
in the smart contract,

00:06:59.070 --> 00:07:01.653
but I found a vulnerability in you.

00:07:02.490 --> 00:07:03.870
And you were right,

00:07:03.870 --> 00:07:05.940
I did take everything from you,

00:07:05.940 --> 00:07:07.577
including the code today.

00:07:07.577 --> 00:07:09.199
(Dio laughs)

00:07:10.080 --> 00:07:13.705
I guess it does run in
the family, brother.

